{"type":"message","id":"21dc3c18","parentId":"1d86690a","timestamp":"2026-04-06T07:00:47.355Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, so workspace-wxlee/.git is a proper git directory (not a file), and it's not a bare repo (core.bare is false in parent repo). But the git status showed it's on branch master with no commits yet.\n\nThe error the user is seeing is typically from `git add` failing when trying to add a submodule or a nested git repo. Let me think...\n\nThe workspace-wxlee directory has no commits, so when the parent repo tries to add it as a submodule or anything like that, it might fail.\n\nActually wait - looking at the error more closely: `error: 'workspace-wxlee/' does not have a commit checked out`. This error comes from `git submodule add` when the source repo doesn't have any commits.\n\nBut actually, the most likely issue is the user is trying to commit changes and git is somehow trying to add the workspace-wxlee directory as part of the staging, and since workspace-wxlee is an empty repo (no commits), it fails.\n\nLet me check if workspace-wxlee is listed in .gitmodules of the parent repo.","thinkingSignature":"1e5983991f49e897d7aa7d1313ca8925a6e11eac62d20ca74b14cec1e29502c9"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_6n67etrkqig1_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/node/.openclaw && cat .gitmodules 2>/dev/null || echo \"No .gitmodules\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"minimax-m2.5:free","usage":{"input":5540,"output":274,"cacheRead":11827,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":17641,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775458840263,"responseId":"06228d18b82311a8afc00b242f8ce9fb"}}
