{"type":"message","id":"13982542","parentId":"09abde42","timestamp":"2026-04-06T12:37:45.571Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking how to add a WeChat account via auth. Looking at the auth-profiles.json files I just read, these contain API keys for AI model providers (minimax, openrouter, google, zai, openai, volcengine), not WeChat credentials.\n\nThe user might be asking about:\n1. How to add WeChat integration/credentials to OpenClaw (for WeChat bot/account)\n2. How to authenticate with WeChat for messaging\n\nLooking at the file structure, I see there's an `openclaw-weixin/` directory which likely handles WeChat integration. Let me check what's there and see if there's documentation or existing config about WeChat accounts.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec:21","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ls -la ~/.openclaw/openclaw-weixin/"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"read:22","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-lucus/AGENTS.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"volcengine-plan","model":"kimi-k2.5","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775479049706,"responseId":"021775479050215d1fe9146833e301f6be5de30142daa10dd9702"}}
